  "_note_reactions": "A `reaction` block is what makes a reaction-cost spell reach the board at all: combat.gd fires the named trigger at the moment it happens and resolves the answer itself, so a reaction is never a button (combat-design.md §2 — zero prompts). `counter` means the trigger's spell unravels on a failed save; `min_level` is how low the reaction stoops, so a 3rd-level slot is not spent to swat a cantrip. Counterspell's numbers come from its catalog description: a Constitution save at DC 10 + the countered spell's level, and a countered caster keeps the slot — the action is the whole cost.",
  "counterspell": {
    "cost": "reaction", "shape": "single", "range_ft": 60, "save": "con",
    "reaction": {"trigger": "spell_cast", "counter": true, "min_level": 1}
  }
